{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the discerning — like the brightness of the firmament</b> — that it receives the light, and the righteous who justify the many, their virtue is great. Therefore he said: <b>like the stars forever and ever</b>, for the virtue of the stars is greater than the virtue of the spheres, even though the firmament is below the spheres."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:24.377980413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}